# CONTRACT_RULES.baseline -- paragraph conservation for the contract corpus.
#
# Generated by `bd-contract-rules --extract` from CLAUDE.md. Each row is a
# normalised, lowercased sha256 prefix of ONE paragraph, plus an excerpt for
# a human. The gate asserts every ACTIVE row is still a paragraph somewhere in
# the corpus (CLAUDE.md, project-knowledge/CONTRACT_CASEBOOK.md), so MOVING a paragraph passes and
# deleting or rewriting one FAILS until it is declared below.
#
# IT MAY ONLY SHRINK BY DECLARATION. Move a row under DECLARED REMOVALS and
# put the reason on the same line -- for a dedupe, name the paragraph that
# survives. DO NOT regenerate this file to clear a failure: regenerating is
# how a lost rule becomes the new baseline, which is the shape bd-mutate hits
# when a battery starts on a dirty tree and adopts the mutant as pristine.
#
# paragraphs: 300

